## What This Preserves (Mathematical Integrity)
- `r.v` (Value) is still computed for every player
- `r.pri` (Priority) = `r.v` - next_pick_value is still calculated correctly
- `wavg(r.v)` is still computed internally for Priority calculation
- Only the VISUAL column is removed from the draft board table

## What Changes Visually
- Draft board table: 9 columns instead of 10 (Player, Pos, Team, OVR, Wins, Priority, Gone, Fills, Action)
- "Value here" column header removed
- "Value here" data cells removed from each row
- Priority column remains and still works correctly (uses r.v internally)

## Verification Steps
1. Load the modified HTML
2. Start a draft
3. Verify draft board has 9 columns (no "Value here" column)
4. Verify Priority values still calculate correctly
5. Verify "Sim to End" completes successfully
6. Verify 100-season simulation works

## Alternative: CSS-only Hide (If Preferred)
If you prefer to keep the DOM structure but hide visually:
```css
/* Add to CSS */
#draftTable2 th[data-sort="value"],
#draftTable2 td.dc-val {
    display: none;
}
```
This keeps DOM structure intact for any JS that might reference column indices.